WEBVTT

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:26.920
Botan!

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:19.490
With you here, Botan,
kick-the-can turns into a crap game!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:23.620
But games like this aren't fun
if you don't take them seriously.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.330
I understand that.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.250
I just wish you'd learn some restraint.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.130
If I kicked it halfheartedly and
it hit someone, it'd be dangerous.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.590
Instead, I'm making it burn
up in the atmosphere.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.300
Are you a human catapult?!

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.470
But that's the fourth can we've lost!

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:42.680
How many cans of coffee are you
gonna make Natsuki drink?!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.430
Why do I have to drink them all myself?!

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.270
<i>Now</i> she gives us a retort!

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.480
I was wondering when you'd jump in.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.320
Whenever I try to yell, I feel like...

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.480
Natsuki?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.690
Are you all right?

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.450
You're the one who wanted
to play kick-the-can, Sakura.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.490
You can't say it's a crap game now...

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.040
Some minutes ago...

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.920
How cute!

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.710
You baked these too, Karin?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.130
Yup, I did!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.290
What do you think?

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.800
They're great!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.710
I'm so happy!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:22.220
Okay! Today, let's play a game
as kids of our generation do!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.850
We're all going to play?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:25.970
Yeah!

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.600
But now that I think about it,
this game only goes up to four players.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.480
I guess someone will be left out!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.610
Sorry, Natsuki!

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.190
Okay. I'll set the traps and bombs,

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.030
and capture monsters once
they're partially destroyed.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.450
Okay. I'm gonna go pick mushrooms.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.530
I'll go gather some honey.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.740
I'm going to practice with the controls.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.540
We just ran out of honey, anyway.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.250
Karin, why are you
cooking meat over there?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.580
Oh, this one's an enemy too, isn't it?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.380
You can tell it's a monster by looking at it!

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.760
Botan, you capture them way too fast.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.760
You fools!

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.760
What's wrong with you?!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.590
Why are you sitting inside playing
video games on such a nice day?

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.350
This is what's wrong with our generation!

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.140
You sure changed your mind quick!

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.600
Ah, but...

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.020
Sakurai, you're the one
who wanted to play a game...

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.900
That isn't what I meant.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.940
Are you a politician now?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.190
I want to play something that
doesn't use electricity,

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.700
like people did in the
days before video games.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.740
P-Play something...
that's not a video game?

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.990
Why do you look genuinely confused?!

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.700
You're making our generation look worse!

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.160
Why don't we exchange love poems?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.830
We don't have to do
something that outdated!

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.710
We don't have to do something
that refined, either!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.090
Then, what should we play?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.550
What should we play?

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.220
W-We should play...

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.690
Kick-the-can!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.690
That's it!

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.190
Today, we'll go to the park
and play kick-the-can!

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.070
And back in the present...

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.700
But now that I think about it...

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.450
Buying coffee from a vending machine

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.410
means we're still using electricity, doesn't it?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.330
That's nitpicking!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.410
You don't have to count that!

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.830
Even though it's coffee in a can...

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.920
...you <b>can</b>not count it!

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:29.090
A-Anyway, I'm giving Botan a handicap
so we won't lose any more cans.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.850
Why do you carry handcuffs around with you?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.730
I'm glad I had my "Apprehending
Creeps Starter Kit" on hand!

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.690
Uh, no. I think using them like
that makes <i>you</i> the creep.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.570
Anyway, Natsuki...

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.740
What?

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.660
Here.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.500
Right!

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.250
Let's resume the game!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.520
Right! Let's resume the game!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.120
I feel... kinda sick...

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.250
What's wrong, Sakura?

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.590
Did you catch a cold?

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.550
Huh? Hey!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.100
Sakura!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.510
Are you okay?!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.900
It appears the first victim has been chosen.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.480
Sinful lambs...

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.440
Welcome to the Little Garden of Judgment.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.530
Now, let us begin.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.320
The ordeal in which you will confront your sins...

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.410
The Game of Judgment:

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.580
Guilty Judge!

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.510
You have all committed a sin.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:19.430
Put hand to breast and try to recall it.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.230
Which one?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.690
No, you need to put your
hand on your own breast!

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.610
She's just turning into a dirty old man now...

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.150
But I have no idea what she's talking about.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.990
Committed a sin?

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.120
What could we have done?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.250
I've repaired everything I've destroyed.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.660
That's true.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.790
Maybe our sin is not catching
fire as a popular anime yet?

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.500
Stop talking about that!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.130
Then, what on earth could it be?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.550
If you don't know, then I shall tell you.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.760
Having the video so eerily
in sync with our conversation

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.260
just makes it more annoying.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:02.890
It happened during "Record 18:
Youth is an Explosion."

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.650
You disregarded your club president, of all people,

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.520
and the four of you played a
video game without her, didn't you?!

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.320
She's really clinging to that grudge.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.440
Leaving out a friend is simply unforgivable!

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.990
Then, why did you kill the
club president first?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.120
I don't understand why you'd do that.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.490
Now, let me explain how this game will work.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.370
Was all that buildup really necessary?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.830
While you were distracted,

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.380
I locked this room from the inside!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.460
What?!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.840
But we're on the inside, right?

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:37.720
She sounded dramatic, but I'm pretty
sure that door opens from the inside.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.390
Does that door even have a lock?

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:45.980
In addition, I have taken the liberty
of affixing bombs somewhere on your bodies.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.730
What?! When?!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:53.480
If you do not fulfill the conditions for
escape and acquire the room key,

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.650
the bombs will explode
and it'll be game over.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.780
Oh, and another thing: The bombs are
invisible to beautiful girls.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:03.990
How could you?!

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:08.210
That means none of us here
can find and disarm the bombs!

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.670
I get it!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.540
That's why you killed Sakura first,

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.670
because she was the only one among
us who could see the bombs!

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.300
What?!

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:27.140
That was just air leaking out of my
lungs and vibrating my vocal cords.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.940
That's one talented corpse.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:33.820
Now, before we begin the game,
there's one thing we must do.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.280
Sorry to make you do this,

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:40.740
but can you please place three
chairs in a circle facing outwards?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.530
So this part's self-service, huh?

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.580
What a pain.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.830
You should be helping us.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:04.640
Now, I will reveal the nature of
the game that shall judge you.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:08.020
It's a game designed to make a
person expose their innermost self.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.390
It's called...

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.100
Musical Chairs!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.940
We know that much.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.360
After she made us set up the chairs,
why is she trying to sound so smart?

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:20.530
When the music stops,
whoever isn't sitting dies!

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.500
She started singing.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.540
What's with this surreal video?

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.750
Looks like we have no choice.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:34.920
Let's play along.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.170
Yeah, why not?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.270
I'm... dead!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.480
Karin.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.320
That's one dead.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.580
How did it feel to sacrifice
your friend to survive?

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.120
Sorry! We all survived!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.830
This is lame. What is she even talking about?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.300
Remove one chair.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.960
Time for the second round!

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:22.470
What?! Even though we all survived?

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.280
And so, the second person dies.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.990
Now, remove one more chair.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:51.540
Who will survive to the end?

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.920
Just one chair now?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.500
Four people on one chair isn't gonna be easy...

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.180
We did it!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:09.600
Well?

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.060
How did it feel to sacrifice
your friends to survive?

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:17.020
Can you live with the pain of
your loneliness from now on?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.520
Hey, Claire, don't you think
you're clutching me a bit too tight?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.070
I don't have a choice!

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.280
Claire, that tickles!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.780
Claire, stop that!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.250
Oh, yeah...

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.330
Did you know there's a pancake festival
going on now at the family restaurant?

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.250
I made reservations for today,
so shall we all go together?

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.540
Hooray!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.130
Pancakes sound good.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:43.760
I've been thinking about them lately.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.510
But making reservations for
a family restaurant seems...

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.180
Oh? Do you think I should have
booked the whole restaurant?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.890
That's not what I meant...

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:26.800
Shall we, then?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.390
Yes!

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.350
Pow!

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.620
The Ancient Art of Hagishirabe-ryuu

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.040
It cut all ties with Hagitsuki-ryuu,

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:06.630
and despite its common origin,
continued to develop along its own path.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:14.390
As time passed, it came to stand opposed
to its parent family, the Hagitsuki-ryuu.

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.930
These days, nobody even
remembers the reason why.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:26.860
And now, the Four Heavenly Kings of
Hagishirabe-ryuu unite under one roof!

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:39.910
So, I'd like to begin

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.580
this regularly-scheduled meeting of the
Hagishirabe-ryuu Four Heavenly Kings.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.550
Does anyone have any business to discuss?

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.590
Nope.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.970
Why do we meet twice a week when
we never have any business to discuss?

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.640
We've totally become regulars at this place.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.680
Hey, they've got new menu items today.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.180
Business...

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.180
I can't think of any...

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.190
Wait, what's with this name?!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.850
Why am I "hopeless"?!

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:08.900
And why is "lover" the word that's
spelled out in red on mine?!

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.700
You don't deny that you love anime, though?

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.740
I don't!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.990
But I can't point out every
single problem at once, can I?!

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.780
I hear you, I hear you.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:21.000
We don't have any business to
discuss, anyway. So let's think...

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:25.000
...of a new nickname for him!

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.090
Hmm...

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.550
The Baseless Genbu!

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.180
That's not any better!

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.970
Something baseless isn't of any use!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.390
Do you prefer Useless Genbu or Pointless Genbu?

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.890
They mean the same thing!

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.520
The Hopeless...

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.310
<i>That's</i> the part you changed?!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.520
That means I'm 100% a burden
to the Four Heavenly Kings!

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:52.900
Byakko, want to split a spinach sauté?

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.490
Sure, let's buzz the waiter.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.740
You're bored of the subject already!

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.410
At least try one more round of suggestions!

00:16:59.030 --> 00:16:59.990
How about...

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:00.870
What?

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.700
Melon soda!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.160
You want me to fetch you some?!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.330
I want cola and orange in a 1:1.618 proportion,
in accordance with the golden ratio.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.130
Your blending instructions are too specific!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:13.260
I hope you shrink your tank top
in the wash, you idiot!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:19.680
By the way, how's our mortal
enemy Hagitsuki-ryuu doing?

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:23.560
Oohagi Botan's club...
The Going Home Club, I think?

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.980
I hear some younger students have joined it.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.610
Mixing cola and orange together is gross!

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.150
Don't complain!

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.940
I hope your headband snaps and
slashes your forehead!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:34.990
That first year...

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.490
I don't like her one bit.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:41.330
When I was monitoring Hagitsuki-ryuu before...

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.950
Botan, that strap is so cute.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:45.830
Hm?

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.210
Oh, this?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.540
You can have it if you want.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.250
What? Are you sure?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.210
Yeah. I've got a whole
bunch of the same one.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:55.590
Wow!

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.800
Now we'll match, Karin!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.800
M-Match?

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.890
You fools!

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:05.100
Wh-What?!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:09.350
Do you know how many stores
I visited to get one like Botan's?!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.730
She says: "It's so cute!"

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.400
and gets it handed to her
by the person herself?!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.440
There's only so much I can
take of this world mocking me!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.610
Why do you have a matching one, too?!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.200
You can buy them on the Net, you know.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.620
You have matching ones, too?!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:24.540
You guys don't secretly love
Hagitsuki-ryuu, do you?!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.200
Huh?!

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.080
No way! She's the enemy!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.000
If I ever met Botan, I'd kill her!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.630
You started using "chan"!

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.750
You're Kokonoe who reserved
a table for five, correct?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.880
I can't wait!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.800
I'm so hungry!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.380
I'm famished after all that crying!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.630
H-Hagitsuki-ryuu!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.350
Fancy seeing you here!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.720
It's been so long!

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.810
Drop in at our dojo again sometime!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.640
We've got a score to settle with you!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:50.730
Here she is!

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:51.770
Finally!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.730
Botan, those people over there...

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.280
Are they friends of yours?

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.940
No, they're my enemies.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:03.030
Float, float, float, float, float!

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:08.790
UFA!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:13.290
The Ancient Art of Hagishirabe-ryuu...

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:22.550
So, I'd like to begin this
week's scheduled meeting.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.260
Any new business?

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.810
Should we talk about
Hagitsuki-ryuu's activities?

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.770
Let's have a report.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.690
I suppose...

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:35.480
It's okay.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.740
They'll remove things like unnatural
light and steam for the DVD release.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.150
That's not the point!

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.530
It's an added perk!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:44.030
Don't take off your tank top all of a sudden!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.950
What if it's not removed from the DVD?

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.200
Don't say that!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.540
What will we do if everyone wants a refund?

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.880
Well, regarding Hagitsuki-ryuu's activities...

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.050
Yes. That's the business at hand.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.600
I want to eat some ice cream!

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.230
You've got everything matching now!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:18.190
Are you sure you don't love
Hagitsuki-ryuu after all?

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:18.940
She's the enemy!

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.360
Fresh Botan!

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:21.820
Smile Botan!

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.150
Stop taking your clothes off!

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:26.490
I hope you get scalped by some
warlike tribe, you spiky-headed jerk!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.660
You fools!

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.000
You're the ones who called her the enemy!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:26.990
Strike! Batter out!

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.610
Change!

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.040
They will return!

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:47.510
When you watched the C part,

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.130
you might be inclined to think
that the Hopeless Genbu's name

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:52.550
was changed to the Baseless Genbu.

00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:54.390
But the truth is, he's still Hopeless.

00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:59.440
We'll show you two others, as well.
